# Sobelow (Phoenix security scanner) - `mix sobelow --config`, run by precommit and CI.
#
# Reviewed false positives are skipped INLINE, with a `# sobelow_skip ["Category.Name"]`
# comment directly above the function that holds the finding. They travel with the
# code, so an edit above them cannot unsuppress them (the old line-based
# .sobelow-skips fingerprint file could, and did). `skip: true` is what makes
# Sobelow read those comments. Every one was read in context:
#   * Traversal.* - paths are built by the app (its data dir, temp files, a
#     bundled catalogue) or looked up by id in the app's own listing before they
#     are touched; no request string is ever joined into a path.
#   * XSS.* - bodies are fixed SVG/PDF/ndjson/escaped-HTML builders or the app's own
#     bundled manual; content types are literals.
#   * DOS.StringToAtom - atoms come from the app's own literals, bundled data or a
#     regex-bounded letter set, never from a request.
#   * CI.System - fixed commands with an argument list (no shell string).
#   * Config.CSWH - the socket origin is checked, but by a function, which
#     Sobelow cannot read: config/config.exs sets check_origin to
#     PolisWeb.HostGuard.origin_allowed?/1, which accepts localhost, 127.0.0.1,
#     ::1, the endpoint url host, and (only with POLIS_LISTEN=lan) this
#     machine's own name and addresses. The same list is a plug at the head of
#     the endpoint that answers 403 to any other Host, so a DNS-rebinding page
#     reaches neither the pages nor the socket (sweep 2026-10-19 POL-1).
#   * Config.CSP - no script-src policy is set; Phoenix's default
#     put_secure_browser_headers is on the browser pipeline. Reported, not fixed:
#     it listens on localhost / behind the operator's own access layer only.
#   * Config.HTTPS - TLS is not this app's job: it listens on localhost / behind the
#     operator's own access layer, and force_ssl in config/prod.exs is not set.
#
# Config.* findings (CSP, CSWH, HTTPS) cannot take an inline comment: Sobelow
# reads them from config files and the router, not from a function. They are
# ignored by name below, on the reasoning in the Config.* bullets above.
[
  exit: :low,
  format: "txt",
  ignore: ["Config.CSP", "Config.CSWH", "Config.HTTPS"],
  ignore_files: [],
  include_mix_tasks: false,
  include_scripts: false,
  out: nil,
  private: false,
  router: nil,
  skip: true,
  summary: false,
  threshold: :low,
  verbose: false
]
